IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cga-types`
IMPORT `cga-scope`
IMPORT `cga-goods`
IMPORT `cga-services`
IMPORT `cga-goal`

-- Consumer Guarantees Act 1993 — TESTS.
-- Expected values are worked from
-- ../registers/source-bundle/act_public_1993_91.txt, not from the code.
-- Amounts are made up, except the s 47 limits.

§ `Tests`

§§ `Helpers`

`a consumer` MEANS Acquirer OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE

GIVEN t IS A `Thing supplied`
GIVETH A Supply
`a supply in trade of` t MEANS Supply OF t, TRUE, FALSE, Date 1 3 2025, NOTHING

-- A goods failure: the guarantee; can it be remedied; did the supplier
-- refuse; is it unsafe (substantial); rejected in time; consequential loss.
-- Price 1000, average retail 900, value with the failure 400.
GIVEN g IS A `Goods guarantee`, remediable IS A BOOLEAN, refused IS A BOOLEAN, unsafe IS A BOOLEAN, `in time` IS A BOOLEAN, loss IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Goods failure`
`goods failure` g remediable refused unsafe `in time` loss MEANS
    `Goods failure` OF g, remediable, refused, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, unsafe, `in time`, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, loss, 1000, 900, 400

-- A service failure: the guarantee; remediable; refused; unsafe; incidental
-- to goods the consumer may reject; a contract; consequential loss.
-- Charge 2000, value of the product 500.
GIVEN g IS A `Service guarantee`, remediable IS A BOOLEAN, refused IS A BOOLEAN, unsafe IS A BOOLEAN, incidental IS A BOOLEAN, contract IS A BOOLEAN, loss IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Service failure`
`service failure` g remediable refused unsafe incidental contract loss MEANS
    `Service failure` OF g, remediable, refused, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, unsafe, FALSE, incidental, contract, loss, 2000, 500

`require` MEANS `require the supplier to remedy the failure within a reasonable time`
`elsewhere` MEANS `have the failure remedied elsewhere and recover the reasonable costs from the supplier`
`reject` MEANS `reject the goods and choose a refund or a replacement`
`value damages` MEANS `damages from the supplier for the reduction in value`
`loss damages` MEANS `damages from the supplier for reasonably foreseeable consequential loss`
`cancel` MEANS `cancel the contract for the service`

§§ `Goal 1 — scope`

-- s 2 consumer
#ASSERT `is a consumer` `a consumer` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `is a consumer` (Acquirer OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `is a consumer` (Acquirer OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `is a consumer` (Acquirer OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `is a consumer` (Acquirer OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE) EQUALS FALSE

-- s 2 goods (c)
#ASSERT `is within the Act as goods, services, or gas and electricity` `a building attached to land, of any other kind` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `is within the Act as goods, services, or gas and electricity` `a building attached to land, easily removable and not designed for residential accommodation` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `is within the Act as goods, services, or gas and electricity` `services` EQUALS TRUE

-- s 43(2)
#ASSERT `the clause validly contracts out under s 43(2)` (`Contracting out clause` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the clause validly contracts out under s 43(2)` (`Contracting out clause` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the clause validly contracts out under s 43(2)` (`Contracting out clause` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the clause validly contracts out under s 43(2)` (`Contracting out clause` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS FALSE

-- ss 41, 43, 56
#ASSERT `the Act gives redress for the supply to` `a consumer` `, supply` (`a supply in trade of` `goods`) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the Act gives redress for the supply to` `a consumer` `, supply` (Supply OF `goods`, FALSE, FALSE, Date 1 3 2025, NOTHING) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the Act gives redress for the supply to` `a consumer` `, supply` (Supply OF `goods`, TRUE, TRUE, Date 1 3 2025, NOTHING) EQUALS FALSE
-- s 41(2) bars redress against the charity only; the manufacturer remains answerable (added after the independent pass)
#ASSERT (`the consumer guarantees position for` (`Consumer case` OF `a consumer`, (Supply OF `goods`, TRUE, TRUE, Date 1 3 2025, NOTHING), `a failure of goods` (`goods failure` `s 6 acceptable quality` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)))'s `remedies against the supplier` EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT (`the consumer guarantees position for` (`Consumer case` OF `a consumer`, (Supply OF `goods`, TRUE, TRUE, Date 1 3 2025, NOTHING), `a failure of goods` (`goods failure` `s 6 acceptable quality` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)))'s `remedies against the manufacturer` EQUALS LIST `damages from the manufacturer for the reduction in value`
#ASSERT `the Act gives redress for the supply to` `a consumer` `, supply` (Supply OF `goods`, TRUE, FALSE, Date 31 3 1994, NOTHING) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the Act gives redress for the supply to` `a consumer` `, supply` (Supply OF `goods`, TRUE, FALSE, Date 1 4 1994, NOTHING) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the Act gives redress for the supply to` `a consumer` `, supply` (Supply OF `goods`, TRUE, FALSE, Date 1 3 2025, JUST (`Contracting out clause` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE)) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the Act gives redress for the supply to` `a consumer` `, supply` (Supply OF `goods`, TRUE, FALSE, Date 1 3 2025, JUST (`Contracting out clause` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE)) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the Act gives redress for the supply to` `a consumer` `, supply` (`a supply in trade of` `a building attached to land, of any other kind`) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the Act gives redress for the supply to` (Acquirer OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE) `, supply` (`a supply in trade of` `goods`) EQUALS FALSE

-- s 47
#ASSERT `the forums for a claim of` 60000 EQUALS LIST `the High Court`, `the District Court`, `the Disputes Tribunal`
#ASSERT `the forums for a claim of` 60001 EQUALS LIST `the High Court`, `the District Court`
#ASSERT `the forums for a claim of` 350000 EQUALS LIST `the High Court`, `the District Court`
#ASSERT `the forums for a claim of` 350001 EQUALS LIST `the High Court`
-- s 46
#ASSERT `the most an assignee or creditor is liable for, claim` 5000 `, owing at the date` 3000 EQUALS 3000
#ASSERT `the most an assignee or creditor is liable for, claim` 5000 `, owing at the date` 8000 EQUALS 5000

§§ `Goal 2 — goods and the supplier`

-- s 16, 17
#ASSERT `the supplier is answerable under Part 2 for` (`goods failure` `s 5 title` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the supplier is answerable under Part 2 for` (`goods failure` `s 11 price` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the supplier is answerable under Part 2 for` (`goods failure` `s 12 repairs and spare parts` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the supplier is answerable under Part 2 for` (`goods failure` `s 13 a manufacturer's express guarantee` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the supplier is answerable under Part 2 for` (`Goods failure` OF `s 6 acceptable quality`, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 1000, 900, 400) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the supplier is answerable under Part 2 for` (`goods failure` `s 7A acceptable quality of gas or electricity` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS TRUE

-- s 21
#ASSERT `the goods failure is of a substantial character` (`goods failure` `s 6 acceptable quality` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the goods failure is of a substantial character` (`goods failure` `s 6 acceptable quality` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the goods failure is of a substantial character` (`Goods failure` OF `s 9 correspondence with description`, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 1000, 900, 400) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the goods failure is of a substantial character` (`Goods failure` OF `s 6 acceptable quality`, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 1000, 900, 400) EQUALS TRUE

-- s 20
#ASSERT `the right to reject still applies to` (`goods failure` `s 6 acceptable quality` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the right to reject still applies to` (`goods failure` `s 6 acceptable quality` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the right to reject still applies to` (`Goods failure` OF `s 6 acceptable quality`, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 1000, 900, 400) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the right to reject still applies to` (`Goods failure` OF `s 6 acceptable quality`, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 1000, 900, 400) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the right to reject still applies to` (`Goods failure` OF `s 6 acceptable quality`, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 1000, 900, 400) EQUALS FALSE

-- s 18(2): can be remedied, not yet refused: require a remedy
#ASSERT `the remedies against the supplier for` (`goods failure` `s 6 acceptable quality` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS LIST `require`
#ASSERT `the remedies against the supplier for` (`goods failure` `s 6 acceptable quality` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS LIST `require`, `loss damages`
-- s 18(2)(b): the supplier refused: elsewhere, or reject
#ASSERT `the remedies against the supplier for` (`goods failure` `s 6 acceptable quality` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS LIST `require`, `elsewhere`, `reject`
-- refused, but too late to reject (s 20)
#ASSERT `the remedies against the supplier for` (`goods failure` `s 6 acceptable quality` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS LIST `require`, `elsewhere`
-- s 18(3): cannot be remedied: reject or damages
#ASSERT `the remedies against the supplier for` (`goods failure` `s 6 acceptable quality` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS LIST `reject`, `value damages`
#ASSERT `the remedies against the supplier for` (`goods failure` `s 6 acceptable quality` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS LIST `value damages`, `loss damages`
-- can be remedied, but substantial (unsafe): (2) and (3) (F1)
#ASSERT `the remedies against the supplier for` (`goods failure` `s 6 acceptable quality` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS LIST `require`, `reject`, `value damages`
-- s 11
#ASSERT `the remedies against the supplier for` (`goods failure` `s 11 price` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS LIST `refuse to pay more than a reasonable price`
-- s 5A: delivery, substantial: reject and damages; not substantial: damages only
#ASSERT `the remedies against the supplier for` (`goods failure` `s 5A delivery` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS LIST `reject`, `loss damages`
#ASSERT `the remedies against the supplier for` (`goods failure` `s 5A delivery` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS LIST `loss damages`
#ASSERT `the remedies against the supplier for` (`goods failure` `s 5A delivery` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS EMPTY
-- s 12 against the supplier: none
#ASSERT `the remedies against the supplier for` (`goods failure` `s 12 repairs and spare parts` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS EMPTY
-- s 7A gas or electricity: as goods
#ASSERT `the remedies against the supplier for` (`goods failure` `s 7A acceptable quality of gas or electricity` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS LIST `reject`, `value damages`

-- s 18(3)(b): 1000 - 400
#ASSERT `the supplier's damages for the reduction in value of` (`goods failure` `s 6 acceptable quality` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS 600
#ASSERT `the supplier's damages for the reduction in value of` (`Goods failure` OF `s 6 acceptable quality`, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 1000, 900, 1200) EQUALS 0

§§ `Goal 3 — goods and the manufacturer`

#ASSERT `the manufacturer is answerable under Part 3 for` (`goods failure` `s 6 acceptable quality` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the manufacturer is answerable under Part 3 for` (`Goods failure` OF `s 6 acceptable quality`, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 1000, 900, 400) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the manufacturer is answerable under Part 3 for` (`Goods failure` OF `s 6 acceptable quality`, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 1000, 900, 400) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the manufacturer is answerable under Part 3 for` (`goods failure` `s 9 correspondence with description` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the manufacturer is answerable under Part 3 for` (`Goods failure` OF `s 9 correspondence with description`, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 1000, 900, 400) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the manufacturer is answerable under Part 3 for` (`goods failure` `s 12 repairs and spare parts` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the manufacturer is answerable under Part 3 for` (`Goods failure` OF `s 12 repairs and spare parts`, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 1000, 900, 400) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the manufacturer is answerable under Part 3 for` (`goods failure` `s 13 a manufacturer's express guarantee` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the manufacturer is answerable under Part 3 for` (`Goods failure` OF `s 13 a manufacturer's express guarantee`, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 1000, 900, 400) EQUALS FALSE
